# Webhook Gateway Architecture Rules

## CRITICAL: Technology Stack Constraints
- Use TaskIQ for async tasks; do not use Celery or FastStream in new code
- Use async/await for all database operations and API endpoints
- Development uses SQLite (aiosqlite) + InMemoryBroker; production uses MySQL + RabbitMQ
- All new code must use uv for dependency management

## File Organization Rules
- API endpoints: place in [app/api/v1/endpoints/](mdc:app/api/v1/endpoints/)
- Database models: modify [app/db/models.py](mdc:app/db/models.py)
- TaskIQ tasks: add to [app/taskiq/tasks.py](mdc:app/taskiq/tasks.py)
- TaskIQ broker: configure in [app/taskiq/broker_manager.py](mdc:app/taskiq/broker_manager.py)
- Configuration: update [app/core/config.py](mdc:app/core/config.py)

## DEPRECATED - Do Not Use
- Do not add new FastStream code or Celery workers
- Use service layer for business logic separation
- Use [app/api/v1/endpoints/ingest.py](mdc:app/api/v1/endpoints/ingest.py) for webhook ingestion

## TaskIQ Dispatch Pattern
When implementing webhook dispatching:
1. Define a task with `@broker.task(task_name="send_webhook_to_subscription")`
2. Enqueue with `await send_webhook_to_subscription.kiq(**kwargs)`
3. In development, InMemoryBroker runs in-process; in production, use RabbitMQ
4. Import broker from [app/taskiq/broker_manager.py](mdc:app/taskiq/broker_manager.py)

## Database Rules
- Always use async SQLAlchemy sessions
- Import session from [app/db/session.py](mdc:app/db/session.py)
- Use soft deletes for subscriptions (set `is_active=False`)
- Store raw webhook payloads as LONGTEXT, not JSON

## Authentication Rules
- Management APIs require Bearer token from `API_KEY` config
- Use `Depends(get_api_key)` for protected endpoints
- Webhook endpoints verify HMAC signatures when source `auth_type` is `signature`
